      "sort_order": 49,
      "block_key": "faq.items",
      "section": "faq",
      "label": "FAQ items",
      "type": "json",
      "metadata": {
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "1. What types of pests commonly infest office environments?",
            "answer_html": "<p>Common office pests include rodents (such as mice and rats), insects like cockroaches, ants, flies, and occasionally bed bugs. These pests can compromise hygiene standards and disrupt daily operations.</p>"
          },
          {
            "question": "2. How can a pest infestation impact my business?",
            "answer_html": "<p>Pest infestations can lead to health code violations, damage to property and equipment, contamination of products, and a tarnished reputation among clients and employees. Addressing pest issues promptly is essential to maintain a safe and professional work environment.</p>"
          },
          {
            "question": "3. What measures can be taken to prevent pests in the office?",
            "answer_html": "<p>Preventive measures include maintaining cleanliness, sealing entry points, proper waste management, and regular inspections. Implementing a comprehensive pest management plan with professional assistance can effectively reduce the risk of infestations.</p>"
          },
          {
            "question": "4. How often should pest control services be scheduled for an office?",
            "answer_html": "<p>The frequency of pest control services depends on factors such as the office's location, size, and history of infestations. Regular inspections, typically quarterly or bi-monthly, are recommended to proactively manage and prevent pest issues.</p>"
          },
          {
            "question": "5. Are the pest control treatments safe for employees and office equipment?",
            "answer_html": "<p>Reputable pest control providers use treatments that are safe for humans and office equipment. It's important to choose a licensed and experienced pest control company that utilizes environmentally friendly and non-disruptive methods.</p>"
          },
          {
            "question": "6. What should I do if I notice signs of a pest infestation in my office?",
            "answer_html": "<p>If you observe signs such as droppings, gnaw marks, or unusual odors, contact a professional pest control service promptly. Early intervention can prevent a minor issue from escalating into a major infestation.</p>"
          }
        ]
      }
